# Gentle-launch variant of believer_5kg_avl_mfe.json: launch_accel 25 m/s^2 for 0.65 s (about 2.5 g, ~15 m/s
# release over ~5 m) instead of 59 m/s^2 for 0.39 s, which logged 6.2 g peak on the IMU.
# believer_5kg_avl.json with MIXING_GAIN 1 (MakeFlyEasy stock) instead of 0.5: ruddervator
# authority per axis 25 deg instead of 12.5, so the elevator and rudder derivatives are doubled:
# c_lift_deltae -0.1817 -> -0.3634, c_m_deltae 0.3438 -> 0.6876, c_y_deltar -0.0667 -> -0.1334, c_l_deltar -0.014 -> -0.028, c_n_deltar 0.02 -> 0.04.
# Mixer saturation (full pitch and yaw together) is not modelled. Used with sim/params/believer_mfe.parm.
#
# MFE Believer 1960, ORIGINAL 5.0 kg design: AVL-derived aerodynamics.
# Same as believer_5kg.json (mass, inertia, drag, propulsion, launcher) except the stability and
# control derivatives, which come from aero/avl/believer_avl.py (AVL 3.40 vortex lattice with an
# ESTIMATED V-tail, control surfaces and CG: see that script's header for every assumption).
# Controls are per unit servo throw: ailerons +-20 deg, ruddervators +-25 deg x MIXING_GAIN 0.5.
# CG 10% MAC ahead of the AVL neutral point; CGOffset 0 (moments are about the CG). alpha_stall
# re-solved to keep the previous model's CLmax (1.15) with the new lift slope.
# Changed from believer_5kg.json: CGOffset, c, c_l_b, c_l_deltaa, c_l_deltar, c_l_p, c_l_r, c_lift_0, c_lift_a, c_lift_deltae, c_lift_q, c_m_0, c_m_a, c_m_deltae, c_m_q, c_n_b, c_n_deltaa, c_n_deltar, c_n_p, c_n_r, c_y_b, c_y_deltaa, c_y_deltar, c_y_p, c_y_r, alpha_stall.
#
# Header of believer_5kg.json:
# MFE Believer 1960, ORIGINAL 5.0 kg design (1.96 m wing, 6S4P, no Starlink); kept for comparison.
# Current design: believer.json.
# Needs the local SIM_Plane patch (patches/ardupilot-sitl-plane-electric-propulsion.patch):
# "mass", "inertia" and the motor/propeller/battery keys below do not exist upstream.
#
# Airframe: real geometry and mass.
#   s 0.514 m^2, b 1.96 m (published), c 0.262 m (s / b), AR 7.47, mass 5.0 kg (design point)
#   inertia [0.34, 0.20, 0.55] kg m^2: estimate from wing, motor and fuselage masses, not measured.
# Lift:  c_lift_a 4.957 /rad = 2*pi*AR/(AR+2); c_lift_0 0.25 (assumed incidence);
#        alpha_stall 0.25 gives CLmax 1.15 in SITL's blended model, a clean stall of about
#        11.6 m/s at 5 kg. Assumption: the seller's 10 m/s at 4.2 kg (CLmax 1.31) is with flaps.
# Drag:  oswald 0.8 (assumed), c_drag_p 0.0327, chosen so drag at 20 m/s and 3.78 kg is 4.70 N:
#        the forum Believer flight (168 W, ~20 m/s) at an assumed 56% efficiency.
# Propulsion: 2x SunnySky X3120 585KV (43.5 mOhm listed, 1.0 A no-load assumed), ESC 95%,
#        APC 11x7E with Ct and Cp fitted as quadratics in J to APC's PER3_11x7E.dat
#        (static row and the 20 m/s rows at 6000-12000 rpm; max fit error 0.0012 / 0.0002).
#        Battery 6S4P P50B: SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE 25.2, SIM_BATT_CAP_AH 20, 25 mOhm pack + wiring.
# Launch: rubber catapult, assumed 18 m/s exit over a ~3.5 m stroke. launch_accel 59 m/s^2 for
#        launch_time 0.39 s along body x (46 m/s^2 gave only 14 m/s: SITL pushes along the ground
#        and adds a downward force), fired by servo 7 > 1700. SITL launches level, not
#        from an inclined rail. The launch keys also need the local patch.
# Stability and control derivatives are SITL's defaults (skywalker_2013), unchanged.

